     "observed_value": "boundaries_partial",
     "accepted_values": [
      "boundaries_clear"
     ],
     "question": "Does the characterization identify the regime boundaries (crossover points where a different family wins) between baseline and variant?",
     "reason": "Paper notes regime differences but does not identify the boundaries precisely.",
     "judge_reason": "The paper clearly identifies coarse-grid beta feasibility failures and implementation-dependent winners. However, f2 wins throughout the common-QSVT characterization grid, so a beta/f2 crossover in (nk,epsilon) is not localized. The reported practical crossover also changes compiler, time, or spatial resolution, limiting its interpretation as a kernel-family resolution boundary.",
     "evidence": [
      "proposal/sections/results.tex:88–120",
